## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a small data-layer primitive using closures, promises, and batching for performance.

## Key Concepts
- Closures and per-key caches
- Promise queuing and batch network calls
- TTL-based eviction and memory safety
- Error handling and cancellation tokens

## Code Example
```javascript
function createBatchingCache(fetcher, { batchDelay = 100, ttl = 5000 } = {}) {
  const cache = new Map(); // key -> { value, expiresAt }
  const inFlight = new Map(); // key -> { promise, resolve, reject }
  let batch = [];
  let timer = null;

  async function flush() {
    const keys = batch;
    batch = [];
    const uniq = Array.from(new Set(keys));
    try {
      const results = await fetcher(uniq);
      uniq.forEach((k, i) => {
        const v = results[i];
        cache.set(k, { value: v, expiresAt: Date.now() + ttl });
        if (inFlight.has(k)) inFlight.get(k).resolve(v);
        inFlight.delete(k);
      });
    } catch (e) {
      uniq.forEach(k => inFlight.get(k)?.reject(e));
      uniq.forEach(k => inFlight.delete(k));
    }
  }

  return {
    get(key) {
      const c = cache.get(key);
      if (c && c.expiresAt > Date.now()) return Promise.resolve(c.value);
      if (inFlight.has(key)) return inFlight.get(key).promise;
      let resolve, reject;
      const p = new Promise((res, rej) => { resolve = res; reject = rej; });
      inFlight.set(key, { promise: p, resolve, reject });
      batch.push(key);
      if (!timer) timer = setTimeout(() => { timer = null; flush(); }, batchDelay);
      return p;
    },
    clear() {
      cache.clear();
      inFlight.clear();
      batch = [];
      if (timer) clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = null;
    }
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical performance optimization skills in real-world scenarios: code splitting, lazy loading strategies, and integrating automated performance validation into CI/CD pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Code splitting: dynamic imports and React.lazy for component-level separation
- Visibility-based loading: IntersectionObserver for on-demand component loading
- Performance budgets: bundle size limits and Core Web Vitals thresholds
- Lighthouse CI: automated performance validation in CI/CD
- Resource optimization: lazy loading for non-critical resources
- User experience: loading states and skeleton screens to prevent layout shifts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dynamic import for analytics chart
const HeavyChart = React.lazy(() => import('./charts/HeavyChart'));

// Visibility gate wrapper
function useVisible(ref) {
  const [visible, setVisible] = React.useState(false);
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => setVisible(entry.isIntersecting),
      { threshold: 0.1 }
    );
    if (ref.current) observer.observe(ref.current);
    return () => observer.disconnect();
  }, [ref]);
  return visible;
}
```

Closures enable functional patterns: private state, currying, and memoization. Trade-offs: closures keep references alive, increasing memory footprint; avoid capturing huge objects. Edge cases: loops with var can close over the wrong index; use let. In UIs, closures can lead to stale state if components re-render without updating bindings; debouncing/memoization illustrate how closures bind behavior to a specific creation context. Debounce example:
```
const debounce = (fn, wait) => {
  let t;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(t);
    t = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), wait);
  };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a robust per-key caching layer with concurrency control and real-time updates, mirroring production frontend concerns in large apps.

## Key Concepts

- Closure-based state encapsulation
- Deduplicating concurrent async calls
- In-flight concurrency control and queuing
- Per-key TTL caching
- Real-time update propagation into cache

## Code Example

```javascript
function createPresenceCache(fetchPresence, { ttl = 30000, maxInFlight = 5, onUpdate } = {}) {
  const cache = new Map();
  const inFlight = new Map();
  const waitQueue = [];

  function drain() {
    if (inFlight.size >= maxInFlight || waitQueue.length === 0) return;
    const next = waitQueue.shift();
    if (!next) return;
    const { userId, resolve } = next;
    const p = fetchPresence(userId).then(status => {
      cache.set(userId, { status, expires: Date.now() + ttl });
      if (onUpdate) onUpdate(userId, status);
      inFlight.delete(userId);
      resolve(status);
      drain();
      return status;
    }).catch(err => { inFlight.delete(userId); throw err; });
    inFlight.set(userId, p);
  }

  async function getPresence(userId) {
    const cached = cache.get(userId);
    if (cached && cached.expires > Date.now()) return cached.status;
    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      waitQueue.push({ userId, resolve, reject });
      drain();
    }).then(status => status);
  }

  function clear(userId) {
    cache.delete(userId);
  }

  return { getPresence, clear };
}
```

